  "result": "Shell completion now handles arguments containing `#`. The shell completion tests pass (59), including a new regression test.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped, so completion saw a truncated command line.\n\n**Fix:** set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character.\n\nI also added `test_split_arg_string_hash` to `tests/test_shell_completion.py` and a note under 8.5.0 in `CHANGES.md`. The changelog entry has no issue or PR number, so you'll want to add one.",
